draw(r--j);

[/asy]
Solution: Only the $8$ corners of the cube have three faces painted red. Each edge has one cube that has $2$ faces painted red. There are $12$ edges, so $12$ cubes have $2$ faces painted red. Each of the six faces has only the center cube painted on exactly $1$ face, and the single cube in the center of the three-inch cube is the only one with no faces painted. We can thus produce the following table: $$
\begin{array}{|c|c|}
\hline
\textbf{Number of red faces} & \textbf{Number of one-inch cubes} \\
\hline
\ast3 & 8 \\
\hline
\ast2 & 12 \\
\hline
1 & 6 \\
\hline
0 & 1 \\
\hline
\multicolumn{2}{|r|}{
\text{Total = 27}}\\
\hline
\end{array}
$$$\ast$ Number of cubes with $2$ or $3$ red faces is $8 + 12 = \boxed{20}.$

